This gamebook features a very simple combat system. There is no strength or stamina because all your heroes are just kids, and it's unlikely that they will achieve success through brute force. Instead, luck is taken into consideration because it invisibly influences everyone's life. Before starting your adventure, roll an ordinary six-sided die (d6) and record the result. This is your luck, and it won't change during the course of the game. If you encounter situations that require you to test your luck, follow the instructions provided in the text. Remember that the success of your adventure depends on your actions, not on dice rolls. As a rule, you will only need to test your luck in case of emergency, when only a miracle can save you. So, make thorough preparations for the adventure. Additionally, write down the names of your companion characters and items you have on your traveler sheet. Do not forget that all characters have their strengths and weaknesses.
Enjoy the game!